==Description== <!--T:23--> 

<!--T:1-->
The '''Revolution''' tool creates a solid by revolving a selected sketch or 2D object about a given axis.

</translate>
[[File:PartDesign Revolution example.svg]]
<translate>

<!--T:11-->
{{Caption|Above: sketch (A) is revolved 270 degrees counter-clockwise around axis (B); resulting solid (C) is shown right.}}

==Usage== <!--T:12-->

<!--T:13-->
# Select a single sketch or one or more faces from the Body.
# There are several ways to invoke the tool:
#* Press the {{Button|[[Image:PartDesign_Revolution.svg|16px]] [[PartDesign_Revolution|Revolve]]}} button.
#* Select the {{MenuCommand|Part Design → Additive Features → [[Image:PartDesign_Revolution.svg|16px]] Revolve}} option from the menu.
# The task panel opens.
# Set the parameters, see [[#Options|Options]] below. {{Version|1.1}}: If the {{MenuCommand|Show interactive draggers when editing features}} [[PartDesign_Preferences#General|preference]] is selected (default), angle parameters can be adjusted with interactive gizmos in the [[3D_View|3D View]].
# Press the {{Button|OK}} button.

==Options== <!--T:24--> 

<!--T:2-->
When creating a revolution, or after double-clicking an existing revolution in the [[Tree_View|Tree View]], the task panel opens. It offers the following settings:

<!--T:25-->
[[Image:partdesign_revolution_parameters.png|frame]]

===Start=== <!--T:61-->

<!--T:62-->
Sets the angular starting position of the revolution around the axis. By default the revolution starts at the sketch or face used as its profile. {{Version|26.3}}
* '''Profile plane''' (default): the revolution starts directly at the profile's sketch plane or face.
* '''Offset''': the revolution starts at an angular offset from the profile, entered in the '''Offset''' field.
* '''Reference''': the revolution starts at a face, [[PartDesign_Plane|datum plane]], or sketch selected with the {{Button|Pick Reference}} button.

This is useful to create multiple features from a single master sketch without needing separate offset planes for each one.

===Direction===

You can select how the revolution is created:
* '''One sided''': the revolution extends on one side of the face.
* '''Two sided''': the revolution extends on both sides of the face. Two sub-menus (Side 1 and Side 2) appear to define the revolution for each side.
* '''Symmetric''': the revolution is symmetrical with respect to the original face.

===Axis=== <!--T:26-->

<!--T:48-->
Specifies the axis of the revolution:

<!--T:10-->
* '''Vertical sketch axis''': selects the vertical sketch axis.
* '''Horizontal sketch axis''': selects the horizontal sketch axis.
* '''Construction line''': selects a construction line from the sketch used by the revolution. The dropdown list will contain an entry for each construction line. The first construction line will be labelled ''Construction line 1''.
* '''Base (X/Y/Z)-axis''': selects the X-, Y- or Z-axis of the Body's origin.
* '''Select reference…''': allows the selection of a straight edge or a [[PartDesign_Line|datum line]] from the Body.

<!--T:49-->
Note that when changing the axis, the '''Reversed''' option may be (un)checked automatically.

===Type=== <!--T:35-->

<!--T:36-->
{{Version|1.0}}

<!--T:37-->
Type offers four different ways of specifying the angle of the revolution:

====Angle==== <!--T:38-->

<!--T:39-->
Enter a numeric value for the '''Angle''' of the revolution. With the '''Direction''' option '''Symmetric''' the revolution will extend half the given angle to either side of the sketch or face.

====To last==== <!--T:40-->

<!--T:41-->
The revolution will extend up to the last face of the support it encounters in its direction. If there is no support, an error message will appear.

====To first==== <!--T:42-->

<!--T:43-->
The revolution will extend up to the first face of the support it encounters in its direction. If there is no support, an error message will appear.

====Up to face==== <!--T:44-->

<!--T:45-->
The revolution will extend up to a face. Press the {{Button|Face}} button and select a face or a [[PartDesign_Plane|datum plane]] from the Body.

===Angle=== <!--T:27--> 

<!--T:15-->
Defines the angle of the revolution. This option is only available if '''Type''' is '''Angle'''. Angles larger than 360° are not possible.

===Project selected axis to profile plane=== <!--T:65-->

<!--T:66-->
{{Version|26.3}}: Projects the selected axis onto the profile plane if the profile is planar (only available for planar profiles). When unchecked (default), the axis is used in its original position and direction.

===Reversed=== <!--T:30-->

<!--T:31-->
Reverses the direction of the revolution.

===Recompute on change===

This option should be checked if '''Show final result''' or '''Show preview overlay''' is checked.

===Show final result===

If checked the cumulative result of the previous features and the current operation is shown.

===Show preview overlay===

If checked the result of the current operation is shown as an overlay.

